menu "Interrupt Configuration"

config STM32_NVIC_PRIORITY_GROUP
    int "NVIC priority grouping"
    default 4
    range 0 4
    help
      NVIC priority grouping configuration.
      Determines how interrupt priority bits are split between
      preemption priority and sub-priority.

      Values:
        0 = NVIC_PRIORITYGROUP_0 (0 bits preemption, 4 bits sub-priority)
        1 = NVIC_PRIORITYGROUP_1 (1 bit preemption, 3 bits sub-priority)
        2 = NVIC_PRIORITYGROUP_2 (2 bits preemption, 2 bits sub-priority)
        3 = NVIC_PRIORITYGROUP_3 (3 bits preemption, 1 bit sub-priority)
        4 = NVIC_PRIORITYGROUP_4 (4 bits preemption, 0 bits sub-priority)

      Recommended: 4 (all bits for preemption priority)

config STM32_SYSTICK_PRIORITY
    int "SysTick interrupt priority"
    default 15
    range 0 15
    help
      SysTick timer interrupt priority (0-15).
      Lower values = higher priority.

      Recommended: 15 (lowest priority) to allow other interrupts
      to preempt SysTick.

config STM32_PENDSV_PRIORITY
    int "PendSV interrupt priority"
    default 15
    range 0 15
    help
      PendSV interrupt priority (0-15).
      Lower values = higher priority.

      Recommended: 15 (lowest priority) for RTOS context switching.

endmenu
